From 98677837849831f94d6fefc0b0534af3fe644812 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:25:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 422/425] hir: a bound associated type is found through a `where Self: Tr`
 supertrait of a local trait

plotters 0.3.7 (sniffnet 1.5.1) src/coord/ranged1d/combinators/group_by.rs:58
`impl<T, R: DiscreteRanged<ValueType = T> + ValueFormatter<T>> ValueFormatter<T> for GroupBy<R>`:
"BUG: ASSERT FAIL: src/hir/hir.cpp:331:path.components().size() > 0u: Invalid path (no nodes) - ::" in
Lifetime Elision. `ValueType` belongs to `Ranged`, and discrete.rs:11 declares the supertrait as a where clause,
`pub trait DiscreteRanged where Self: Ranged`. from_ast's find_source_trait_ast (which trait defines a bound
associated type, for a trait of the current crate) searched the trait's `: Supertrait` list only, so the binding's
source trait stayed empty (`ValueType{::}=T`) and the Lifetime Elision visitor looked up the empty path. The HIR
side was already right: bind.cpp's m_all_parent_traits includes `where Self:` bounds for extern traits.

find_source_trait_ast now also walks the trait's IsTrait bounds whose type lowers to `Self` (skipping the trait
itself), the same recursion as for listed supertraits. An associated type that no supertrait defines is
an error (rustc's E0220) instead of the later assert, in both the `Assoc = T` and the `Assoc: Bound` arms;
the latter had that error commented out.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
---

diff --git a/src/hir/from_ast.cpp b/src/hir/from_ast.cpp
index 65272e81..6e50e8bb 100644
